  <running_head>HORRENDA EXEMPLA</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l>Præbe laudes personare,</l>
    <l>Gaudia tua decantare,</l>
    <l>Nulla vox nec lingua quarę</l>
    <l>Plenè te sufficit laudare.</l>
    <l>Gaude, cum Angelo saris,</l>
    <l>A pneumate fœcundaris,</l>
    <l>Lucidior es stella maris,</l>
    <l>Et verus splendor solaris.</l>
    <l>Ave cum gratiâ plena,</l>
    <l>Recepisti mente serenâ,</l>
    <l>Et concepisti filium,</l>
    <l>O quantum tibi gaudium!</l>
    <l>Gaude Engaddina vitis,</l>
    <l>Culta pulchris margaritis,</l>
    <l>Botrum dulcem paris mitis,</l>
    <l>Fugantem malum aspidis.</l>
    <l>Porta nunc Ezechielis</l>
    <l>Claufa fuisti fidelis,</l>
    <l>Quando creator de cœlis</l>
    <l>Exivit claustris non læsis.</l>
    <l>Gaude quòd tres Magi sagi</l>
    <l>Tribus donis bonis quærunt,</l>
    <l>Aurum, thus, myrrham ferentes,</l>
    <l>Deum verum natum,</l>
    <l>Gnatum tuum, suum Regem,</l>
    <l>Legem viæ à stella rimantes.</l>
    <l>Gaude, quòd ad templum isti,</l>
    <l>Natum tuum obtulisti,</l>
    <l>A vidua didicisti,</l>
    <l>Et à Propheta audisti</l>
    <l>Bene</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Printed text is Latin verse in roman type; a few letters are damaged by wear. "Bene" at the lower right is the start of the following word, cut off at the page edge. The running head reads "HORRENDA EXEMPLA" with the number 178 printed at the top left.</notes>
